+
+##### Active long-term memory in this local DSH build
+
+This local build retrieves memory for **each user turn**, using the current message as the query,
+and injects the result before the model answers. A topic change therefore triggers its own retrieval.
+Tool-only continuation steps do not retrieve again. Replies are automatically retained at turn stop;
+Hindsight performs extraction and consolidation asynchronously, so newly saved facts become searchable
+after the server processes them. This does not require the model to decide to call a memory tool.
+The existing tools remain available for deliberate searches, deeper reflection and corrections.
+
+The policy lives in the package root's [`dsh-memory.config.json`](./dsh-memory.config.json):
+
+| Setting | Shipped value | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `autoInject` | `"recall"` | Retrieve facts directly; `reflect`, `pages`, and `none` remain available |
+| `autoInjectEveryTurns` | `1` | Retrieve every user turn; `N` retrieves on turns 1, 1+N, etc.; `0` keeps the original session-start behavior |
+| `injectTimeoutMs` | `7000` | Deadline for automatic recall/page search, in milliseconds |
+| `recallOptions.types` | `["observation", "world", "experience"]` | Include consolidated knowledge and extracted facts that have not yet been consolidated |
+| `recallOptions.max_tokens` | `2000` | Server-side recall response token budget |
+| `recallOptions.budget` | `"low"` | Retrieval search budget |
+| `retainSessions` | `true` | Automatically retain conversations |
+| `autoUpdate` | `false` | Keep this local runtime from checking npm for updates |
+
+These DSH defaults load after the existing environment compatibility layer and before
+`~/.hindsight/coding-agent.json`. Explicit settings in that file, `harnesses.dsh`, `paths` and `banks`
+continue to override them. No new environment variables are introduced. A missing or malformed root
+policy file is a configuration error. Include it when copying this plugin offline.
+
+An empty recall or an earlier failed request does not stop future scheduled retrievals. Identical
+results are injected again because older injected messages may have left the model's context during
+compaction. Retrieved context is excluded from automatic transcript retention.
+
+Restart DSH to load code changes. Policy changes apply when the runtime is recreated (on restart,
+or via the local manager's `runtime.refresh()`). The published settings-only manager requires a
+restart. This is a local change to `dist/dsh.js`; reinstalling or rebuilding the upstream package
+replaces it. The other bundled agent adapters retain their upstream behavior.
 
